Fallible waits need finite bounds. Carry the caller’s remaining deadline across [service](/lore/services-capture-dependencies) boundaries rather than granting each hop a fresh full wait.

> The timeout is a simple mechanism allowing you to stop waiting for an answer once you think it will not come.

Source: [Q05](/lore/durability-bibliography#q05); [B4](/lore/durability-bibliography#b4-release-it), [B12](/lore/durability-bibliography#b12-site-reliability-engineering).

## Failure it prevents

Abandoned requests occupy resources while their downstream calls continue.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`Effect.timeout` and timeoutOption support local timeout policy. Protocols must carry deadline and cancellation. Foreign operations must cooperate with interruption.

Source: `packages/effect/src/Effect.ts`.

## How to check

Delay the dependency past the deadline. Check released capacity and reconcile any uncertain remote write. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Retry load needs a budget](/lore/retry-load-needs-a-budget), [Retry needs idempotent effects](/lore/retry-needs-idempotency).

